# Git & Agile

## Branch Naming
- MUST use: `feature/<JIRA-123>-<short-slug>` (e.g. `feature/FUXA-42-modbus-timeout`)
- Bug fixes: `fix/<JIRA-123>-<short-slug>`
- Docs only: `docs/<short-slug>`
- TODO: confirm with team — `CONTRIBUTING.md` shows `feature/my-feature` without JIRA prefix

## Commits
- MUST use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/): `type(scope): description`
- Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `test`, `chore`
- Example: `fix(api): reject expired JWT before project load`
- MUST write clear, single-purpose commits; one logical change per commit

## Pull Requests
- MUST fill `.github/pull_request_template.md` checklist
- MUST NOT include `client/dist/`, `node_modules/`, or `server/_appdata/` files
- SHOULD keep PRs under ~400 changed lines; split larger work
- MUST open an issue first for major/architectural changes (`CONTRIBUTING.md`)

## Definition of Done
- [ ] Code follows 4-space indent and project style
- [ ] `cd server && npm test` passes (if server touched)
- [ ] `cd client && npm run lint` passes (if client touched)
- [ ] Auth/security changes include `server/test/authorization/` test
- [ ] Docs updated in `docs/` when user-facing behavior changes
- [ ] No build artifacts committed
- [ ] Tested locally (backend :1881 + browser)

## User Story Format
```
As a <role>, I want <capability>, so that <benefit>.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Given <precondition>, When <action>, Then <outcome>
- Given <precondition>, When <action>, Then <outcome>
```
